# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ChromaDB persistent store (runtime, not committed). backend/data/* (not
# backend/data/, no trailing wildcard) is deliberate — git can't re-include
# a file via a negation pattern below if the parent directory itself is
# excluded (a real, confirmed git limitation, not a style choice); this
# excludes the directory's contents individually instead, which negation
# patterns actually can override.
backend/data/*
!backend/data/curated_examples.jsonl
!backend/data/template_embeddings.json

# Generated meme output (runtime artifacts)
backend/static/generated/*.png
backend/static/generated/*.jpg

# Fonts (add your own — not committed)
backend/fonts/*.ttf
backend/fonts/*.otf

# Next.js
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.env*.local
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# pytest
.pytest_cache/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Docker volumes (runtime — model weights, ChromaDB, generated PNGs)
volumes/

# Claude Code — skills/hooks/settings.json are shared harness config and
# travel with the repo; settings.local.json (personal permission
# allowlist) and other local-only state stay ignored. `.claude/*` (not
# `.claude/`) is deliberate — same reasoning as backend/data/* above: a
# bare directory line excludes the whole tree before any negation pattern
# is even considered.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json

# A skill's own driver dependencies (e.g. run-memegpt's Playwright
# install) aren't part of the skill's tracked content — same reasoning
# as frontend/node_modules below. package.json/package-lock.json still
# get tracked via the !.claude/skills/ negation above.
.claude/skills/*/node_modules/

# Large Kaggle dataset files (download separately, not committed).
# Anchored to the repo root (/data/, not data/) — an unanchored pattern
# here also matched backend/data/ (a different directory, ChromaDB's own
# ignore rule a few lines up already covers it), which silently blocked
# backend/data/template_embeddings.json from ever being added despite its
# own explicit negation exception below.
/data/
memes.json
memes_data.tsv
memes_reference_data.tsv

# sed backup files
*.bak

# Working prompts written TO an AI coding agent (second-person imperative
# instructions, e.g. "wait for my approval before writing any code") — kept
# locally for reference, deliberately not part of the public repo alongside
# README.md/CLAUDE.md's polished documentation.
memegpt-growth-master-prompt.md
memegpt-lore-mode-spec.md
memegpt-multimodal-master-prompt.md
CLAUDE_CODE_SETUP.md
FRONTEND_MASTER_PROMPT.md
MEMEGPT_MASTER.md

# Feasibility write-up tied to the removed multimodal prompt file above —
# a legitimate engineering decision record, but its opening line cites
# that file by name, which is a dangling reference once it's not public.
# Kept locally for reference, same as the prompt files themselves.
FEASIBILITY.md

# CLAUDE.md — the working context/instructions file an AI coding agent
# reads at the start of every session in this repo. Genuinely useful for
# that purpose, but written in session-log voice (dated incident
# narration, repeated references to "the project owner," design-approval
# anecdotes) rather than as public documentation — same category as the
# prompt files above, just much larger. Kept locally so agent sessions in
# this working directory keep full context; never pushed.
CLAUDE.md

# docs/DECISIONS.md — CLAUDE.md's narrative (design history, incidents,
# rejected approaches), moved here verbatim. Same reason CLAUDE.md itself
# is local-only. Kept for agent sessions; never pushed.
docs/DECISIONS.md

# Two runbooks with real, useful setup instructions, but written
# second-person from the AI agent to the repo owner (one literally
# addresses "me," the agent) rather than as public docs. Kept locally.
docs/DISCORD_SETUP.md
docs/FINETUNE_RUNBOOK.md

# Vercel CLI's local project link metadata + env files (added automatically
# by `vercel link`) — .env/.env.local/.env.*.local above already cover real
# env files elsewhere; this was previously two unanchored rules (`.vercel`
# and a bare `.env*`) that silently blocked every .env.example anywhere in
# the repo from ever being tracked, not just this directory.
.vercel/
.env*

# Terraform (terraform/ has its own .gitignore too — belt and suspenders
# in case a *.tfvars-style file ever gets created outside that directory)
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
